# Day 10 — the build context is contract-platform/ only. Everything below stays on the laptop.
#
# Two reasons, one of them security:
#   1. Credentials. Day 09 moved every credential into Secrets Manager; a stray .env or
#      application-local.yaml sent in the build context could be COPY'd into a layer, and a
#      layer is forever — deleting the file in a later layer does not remove it from the image.
#   2. Speed and determinism. target/ is rebuilt inside the image; shipping a stale local one
#      is at best wasted upload and at worst a confusing mismatch.

# build output and tool state
target/
.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar
platform.log
*.log

# credential material — mirrors the root .gitignore (Day 09)
.env
.env.*
*.env
secrets.json
secrets.local.json
application-local.yaml
application-local.yml
*-local.yaml
*-local.yml
.aws/
*.pem
*.p12
id_rsa*

# IDE / OS noise
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
.DS_Store
HELP.md

# the image's own build files are not inputs to the build
Dockerfile
.dockerignore